From 855ef7f678513b99a43433d252b06bda26083bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:20:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] CA-430074: Network.create lets vm-admin reconfigure
 dom0 IP and HIMN listener

The minimum allowed role of invoking Network.create is vm-admin. But the
[other_config] map of a Network object (except the key specified by
[map_keys_roles]) are of minimum role of pool-operator. So the [other_config]
parameter of Network.create should be checked to not allow two
particular keys which might impact the host internal management network
(HIMN) when the caller of the API is of vm-admin role. The HIMN is
allowed to be managed with pool-operator or higher privilege levels.

Additionally, there is another path (import) to get the privilege
escalation happen. When VM.import decides to create a network that
doesn't exist on this pool, the original bridge is meaningless to this
pool. So make Network.create choose the bridge, and always create a
managed network. This also eliminates the bypass of the
bridge_blacklist.

Includes unit tests for the per-key RBAC check on maps of Network, and
the corresponding last_known_schema_hash update.

This is CVE-2026-102707, part of XSA-530.

Signed-off-by: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Reviewed-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
